  "type": "heading_2",
  "heading_2": {
   "rich_text": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": {
      "content": "What multi-agent systems do differently",
      "link": null
     },
     "annotations": {
      "bold": true,
      "italic": false,
      "strikethrough": false,
      "underline": false,
      "code": false,
      "color": "default"
     },
     "plain_text": "What multi-agent systems do differently",
     "href": null
    }
   ],
   "is_toggleable": false,
   "color": "default"
  },
  "archived": false
 },
 {
  "object": "block",
  "id": "56c41818-9447-4c5c-8a67-a3ee31fefbde",
  "parent": {
   "type": "page_id",
   "page_id": "36894183-19f3-80a0-9d7a-db2e47c3849e"
  },
  "created_time": "2026-06-10T04:21:00.000Z",
  "last_edited_time": "2026-06-10T04:21:00.000Z",
  "created_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "231d872b-594c-81f2-a375-0002b8783aca"
  },
  "last_edited_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "231d872b-594c-81f2-a375-0002b8783aca"
  },
  "has_children": false,
  "in_trash": false,
  "type": "paragraph",
  "paragraph": {
   "rich_text": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": {
      "content": "A multi-agent system distributes the cognitive load that overwhelms a single agent across multiple specialised models. Instead of one agent attempting to be a financial analyst, a regulatory expert, a risk assessor, and a communication writer simultaneously, the system assigns each role to a dedicated agent with its own focused system prompt, its own constrained toolset, and its own isolated context window.",
      "link": null
     },
     "annotations": {
      "bold": false,
      "italic": false,
      "strikethrough": false,
      "underline": false,
      "code": false,
      "color": "default"
     },
     "plain_text": "A multi-agent system distributes the cognitive load that overwhelms a single agent across multiple specialised models. Instead of one agent attempting to be a financial analyst, a regulatory expert, a risk assessor, and a communication writer simultaneously, the system assigns each role to a dedicated agent with its own focused system prompt, its own constrained toolset, and its own isolated context window.",
     "href": null
    }
   ],
   "icon": null,
   "color": "default"
  },
  "archived": false
 },
 {
  "object": "block",
  "id": "37b94183-19f3-801b-a8bb-ef6a32f5c162",
  "parent": {
   "type": "page_id",
   "page_id": "36894183-19f3-80a0-9d7a-db2e47c3849e"
  },
  "created_time": "2026-06-10T04:21:00.000Z",
  "last_edited_time": "2026-06-10T04:21:00.000Z",
  "created_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "231d872b-594c-81f2-a375-0002b8783aca"
  },
  "last_edited_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "231d872b-594c-81f2-a375-0002b8783aca"
  },
  "has_children": false,
  "in_trash": false,
  "type": "paragraph",
  "paragraph": {
   "rich_text": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": {
      "content": "Each specialised agent operates within a context window that contains only the information relevant to its specific role. The credit risk agent sees credit data and risk models. It does not see the regulatory compliance analysis or the draft client communication. Its context is smaller, more focused, and its reasoning is correspondingly more reliable.",
      "link": null
     },
     "annotations": {
      "bold": false,
      "italic": false,
      "strikethrough": false,
      "underline": false,
      "code": false,
      "color": "default"
     },
     "plain_text": "Each specialised agent operates within a context window that contains only the information relevant to its specific role. The credit risk agent sees credit data and risk models. It does not see the regulatory compliance analysis or the draft client communication. Its context is smaller, more focused, and its reasoning is correspondingly more reliable.",
     "href": null
    }
   ],
   "icon": null,
   "color": "default"
  },
  "archived": false
 },
 {
  "object": "block",
  "id": "37b94183-19f3-8038-a5c5-fd1feedd1498",
  "parent": {
   "type": "page_id",
   "page_id": "36894183-19f3-80a0-9d7a-db2e47c3849e"
  },
  "created_time": "2026-06-10T04:21:00.000Z",
  "last_edited_time": "2026-06-10T04:22:00.000Z",
  "created_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "231d872b-594c-81f2-a375-0002b8783aca"
  },
  "last_edited_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "231d872b-594c-81f2-a375-0002b8783aca"
  },
  "has_children": false,
  "in_trash": false,
  "type": "paragraph",
  "paragraph": {
   "rich_text": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": {
      "content": "Independent tasks can also be assigned to multiple agents simultaneously rather than sequentially. This reduces the total processing time for complex multi-step assessments. ",
      "link": null
     },
     "annotations": {
      "bold": false,
      "italic": false,
      "strikethrough": false,
      "underline": false,
      "code": false,
      "color": "default"
     },
     "plain_text": "Independent tasks can also be assigned to multiple agents simultaneously rather than sequentially. This reduces the total processing time for complex multi-step assessments. ",
     "href": null
    }
   ],
   "icon": null,
   "color": "default"
  },
  "archived": false
 },
 {
  "object": "block",
  "id": "37b94183-19f3-8014-b3db-feeabd29ec4e",
  "parent": {
   "type": "page_id",
   "page_id": "36894183-19f3-80a0-9d7a-db2e47c3849e"
  },
  "created_time": "2026-06-10T04:22:00.000Z",
  "last_edited_time": "2026-06-10T04:22:00.000Z",
  "created_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "231d872b-594c-81f2-a375-0002b8783aca"
  },
  "last_edited_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "231d872b-594c-81f2-a375-0002b8783aca"
  },
  "has_children": false,
  "in_trash": false,
  "type": "callout",
  "callout": {
   "rich_text": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": {
      "content": "Multi-agent systems are not a single architecture. They are a family of patterns, each appropriate for a different class of problem. You do not need to understand how to build these; only that they exist and what problem each one solves.",
      "link": null
     },
     "annotations": {
      "bold": false,
      "italic": false,
      "strikethrough": false,
      "underline": false,
      "code": false,
      "color": "default"
     },
     "plain_text": "Multi-agent systems are not a single architecture. They are a family of patterns, each appropriate for a different class of problem. You do not need to understand how to build these; only that they exist and what problem each one solves.",
     "href": null
    }
   ],
   "icon": {
    "type": "emoji",
    "emoji": "\u27a1\ufe0f"
   },
